From: Agent Browser contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Android product input: tolerate touch-sequence latch overlap

Device-verified failure on r13t (OnePlus PKG110): switching tabs while a page
touch sequence is still latched detaches the content surface mid-touch, the
TouchEnd never arrives, and the next TouchStart crashes the renderer:
  FATAL cc/input/input_handler.cc:2689 DCHECK failed:
  !is_handling_touch_sequence || !is_handling_touch_sequence_
-> frozen content, then PRE_ANR.

Official Chrome release builds compile this DCHECK out and tolerate the
overlap; this build runs with DCHECKs enabled, so the product keeps the
latch instead of crashing (the sequence end clears it) and always applies
the false transition.

--- a/cc/input/input_handler.cc
+++ b/cc/input/input_handler.cc
@@ -2685,8 +2685,14 @@
 }
 
 void InputHandler::SetIsHandlingTouchSequence(bool is_handling_touch_sequence) {
-  // We should not attempt to start handling a touch sequence twice.
-  DCHECK(!is_handling_touch_sequence || !is_handling_touch_sequence_);
+  // The product's tab/env switch can detach the content surface mid-touch, so
+  // a TouchEnd may never arrive and the latch stays true into the next
+  // sequence. Official release builds compile this DCHECK out and tolerate
+  // exactly that overlap; keep the latch instead of crashing the renderer
+  // (the sequence end clears it), and always apply the false transition.
+  if (is_handling_touch_sequence && is_handling_touch_sequence_) {
+    return;
+  }
   is_handling_touch_sequence_ = is_handling_touch_sequence;
 }
 
